.\" Man page for mount-wrapper — install as /usr/share/man/man1/mount-wrapper.1
.TH MOUNT-WRAPPER 1 "2026-07" "mount-wrapper" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mount-wrapper \- archive auto-mounter orchestrator (ratarmount engines)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mount-wrapper
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mount-wrapper
discovers archives under configured source directories, indexes and mounts them
via external ratarmount engines (default
.BR ratarmount-rs ),
runs first-mount hooks, and exposes a Unix control socket plus an optional
localhost HTTP API and embedded operator SPA.
.PP
It does
.B not
reimplement ratarmount inside Go. Engines, FUSE userland, and optional convert
tools must be installed separately.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print version, commit, and build date.
.TP
.B help
Show usage summary.
.TP
.B serve
Run the daemon (scan / index / mount / hooks loop). Loads YAML config, opens
the state database, binds the control socket when configured, and optionally
starts the HTTP API when
.B web_enabled
is true.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Config YAML (default: platform path, e.g.
.IR /etc/mount-wrapper/config.yaml
on Linux).
.TP
.B \-\-once
Run a single service tick then exit (tests / oneshot debug).
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-unauth
Allow control-plane ops without peer credentials. Also enabled when env
.B MOUNT_WRAPPER_CONTROL_ALLOW_UNAUTH=1
.RE
.TP
.B doctor
Offline environment diagnostics (FUSE, bins, paths, disk, peercred notes).
Does not require a running
.B serve
process.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable report.
.TP
.B \-\-fix\-systemd
Write a systemd drop-in for source paths (when applicable).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Config to diagnose.
.RE
.TP
.B config show|set
Show or update configuration.
.RS
.TP
.B show \-\-local
Read the config file only (no control socket).
.TP
.B set
Apply a full config or shallow patch via the running daemon, or offline with
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
Flags:
.BR \-\-json ,
.BR \-\-file ,
.BR \-\-patch ,
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
.RE
.TP
.B status
Service status (requires
.BR serve ).
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output;
.B \-\-sizes
includes size metrics (slower).
.TP
.B metrics [\fIARCHIVE_ID\fR]
Archive size metrics (requires
.BR serve ).
.TP
.B rescan
Trigger an immediate source scan (requires
.BR serve ).
.TP
.B retry \fIARCHIVE_ID\fR
Reset mount attempts for one archive (requires
.BR serve ).
.TP
.B mount \fIPATH\fR
Request mount of an archive path (requires
.BR serve ).
.TP
.B unmount \fITARGET\fR|\-\-all
Unmount managed archive(s) (requires
.BR serve ).
.TP
.B purge \fIARCHIVE_ID\fR
Purge state/index/overlay for an archive. Requires
.B \-\-yes
and a running
.BR serve .
.TP
.B hooks list|status
Inspect first-mount hooks (requires
.BR serve ).
.TP
.B reload
Reload configuration from disk (control
.B reload
op / SIGHUP equivalent). Applies hot-reloadable keys such as
.BR log_level ,
.BR source_dirs ,
and
.BR use_inotify
(inotify watches are restarted). Requires a running
.BR serve .
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Config YAML path.
.TP
.BR \-\-socket " " \fIPATH\fR
Control socket path (overrides
.B control_socket
in config) for socket-backed CLI commands.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Primary file:
.I /etc/mount-wrapper/config.yaml
(Linux FHS). Schema version 1. Hot-reloadable keys apply on
.B reload
/ SIGHUP without a full process restart;
.BR web_enabled ,
.BR web_token ,
.BR web_host ,
.BR web_port ,
and path keys require process restart (HTTP bind and token are fixed at serve start).
See packaged examples under
.I /usr/share/mount-wrapper/
or the source tree
.IR packaging/examples/ .
.PP
Important security-related keys:
.TP
.B web_enabled / web_host / web_port / web_token
HTTP API + SPA. Default bind is loopback. Empty
.B web_token
means no Bearer auth (acceptable only on trusted loopback).
Changing any of these four keys requires a process restart.
When the web server is on,
.B GET /metrics
exposes Prometheus text gauges; scrapes on loopback need no token.
.TP
.B log_level
Daemon slog verbosity (DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR, CRITICAL). Hot-reloaded.
Overridden while
.B MOUNT_WRAPPER_LOG_LEVEL
is set to a valid level.
.TP
.B control_socket
Unix socket path for CLI and local control.
.TP
.B hooks_dir
Directory of first-mount hook executables (must pass owner/writable/realpath
checks).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MOUNT_WRAPPER_CONTROL_ALLOW_UNAUTH
When set to
.BR 1 ,
allows control connections without peer credentials (default off). Prefer
fix/group socket auth in production.
.TP
.B MOUNT_WRAPPER_LOG_LEVEL
When set to a valid level (DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR, CRITICAL), overrides
config
.B log_level
for the serve process at start and on each config reload. Invalid values are
ignored. See
.I packaging/env.example
for a sample EnvironmentFile.
.TP
.B WSL_DISTRO_NAME
Used by the HTTP
.B /api/wsl-info
helper for Windows UNC path hints.
.PP
Hook processes receive
.B MOUNT_WRAPPER_*
variables only for archive and config fields (no dual
.B TARMOUNT_*
export from this daemon). Engine-specific variables such as
.B RATARMOUNT_*
may still be set for child mount processes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mount-wrapper/config.yaml
Main configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/mount-wrapper/hooks.d/
First-mount hooks.
.TP
.I /var/lib/mount-wrapper/
Mounts, indexes, overlays, state database.
.TP
.I /run/mount-wrapper/control.sock
Default control socket (mode 0660).
.TP
.I /run/mount-wrapper/
Runtime directory (socket + pidfile).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B non-zero
Usage error, config/load failure, or command/service failure.
.SH SECURITY
Control socket authentication uses peer credentials (root or group
.BR mount-wrapper ).
The HTTP API defaults to loopback with optional Bearer token. Destructive HTTP
actions (purge, unmount-all, rescan) are rate-limited per client. See
.I docs/security.md
in the source distribution for a full review of hooks path escape, token
defaults, and escape hatches.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fusermount3 (1),
ratarmount / ratarmount-rs documentation.
.PP
Project docs:
.IR https://github.com/hilather/mount-wrapper
